<strong>1.3</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">All software (aircraft, panels, textures, scenery, software, etc.) made available to members through Air Inter Virtual Airlines (download or otherwise) is strictly reserved for company members and must be redistributed without prior consent for the VA Director.</span></span></div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><br />
<strong>1.4</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">As the principle of Air Inter Virtual Airlines is based on trust, no cheating will be tolerated.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span><span style=\"color: #333399\"></span><br />
<br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><strong>1.5</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">In the event of cheating, the staff of Air Inter Virtual Airlines will take the appropriate measures (which may include exclusion of the person concerned); in the event of a dispute, the final decision rests with the Director of the airline.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span></div>

<div style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>1.6</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Under no circumstances may Air Inter Virtual Airlines, its Director and/or members of the staff and/or ARIT (Association of Former Air Inter Employees) be held responsible and/or prosecuted for any reason whatsoever.</span></span></div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>1.7</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">In the event of refusal, disobedience, cheating, bad faith or any other malicious act and/or behavior contrary to the MANEX and MANOPS regulations, or which may harm the brand image of Air Inter Virtual Airlines and/or ARIT (Association of Former Air Inter Employees) and/or Air Inter, sanctions will be taken by the staff members against the persons concerned (which may include exclusion); in the event of a dispute, the final decision rests with the Director of the airline.</span></span></div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>1.8</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Reserved.</span></span><br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>1.9</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">While flying online, the rules of good conduct as well as all procedures described in the IVAO and VATSIM information and/or instruction manuals shall be followed.</span></span><br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>1.9.1</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Each member undertakes to complete at least one flight (one PIREP filed and validated) every 60 days in order to maintain active member status. If no flight is validated within 60 days, the status will automatically become inactive and, in this case, the person concerned will be set aside from the VA (except for exceptional reasons and after mutual agreement of the staff). However, inactive members and/or those set aside from the VA may submit a request to regain active status within the VA (at the discretion of the staff members and depending on the motivation of the requesting member).</span></span><br />
&nbsp;</div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><strong>1.9.2</strong>&nbsp;-&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Each member&nbsp;agrees to use the automatic flight reporting system (ACARS). In cases of impossibility (e.g., ACARS program incompatible with the simulator used, etc.), the flight report must be submitted manually via the Operations Control Center - OCC.</span></span><br />
&nbsp;</div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"></span></span>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong>1.9.3</strong> - <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Minimum required hours to progress through the different periods and access the 2 subsidiaries:</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"></span></p>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span>Newly hired pilot: The newly hired pilot is on probation for the first&nbsp;10 flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Flight Engineer: 10 flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">First Officer: 100</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Captain: 200</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> flight hours</span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">Instructor : 500</span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> flight hours</span><br />
	&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium\"><strong>1.9.4</strong> - <span style=\"font-size:16px;\">In addition to the minimum required flight hours, progression through the different periods may be done, if necessary, after consultation among staff members to evaluate, in particular</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\">:</span></span></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<ul>
	<li>Conduct on the IVAO and/or VATSIM network and overall motivation.</li>
	<li>Respect for the brand image of Air Inter, Air Inter Virtual Airline, and ARIT.</li>
	<li>Participation in VA life: network flights, Fly-ins, general presence (forum, Discord, etc.).</li>
	<li>Compliance with company procedures (FOM/AOM) and IVAO/VATSIM procedures/regulations.<br />
	&nbsp;</li>
</ul>

<p></p>
</div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"></span></div>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">2-REGISTRATION</span></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>2.0</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Any person who applies may become a member of Air Inter Virtual Airlines. The applicant must demonstrate overall motivation, e.g. regularity and seriousness of flights, participation in VA life, forum activity, participation in fly-in events, general discussions, interest in Air Inter and aviation in general, etc...</span></span><br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>2.1</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">The Director of Air Inter Virtual Airlines reserves the right to admit a member, refuse an application, and/or dismiss a member if this proves necessary for the proper operation and/or brand image of Air Inter Virtual Airlines and/or ARIT (Association of Former Air Inter Employees) and/or Air Inter.</span></span></p>

<div style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>2.2</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">After acceptance of the registration application, new members must register in&nbsp;</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\">the Operations Control Center - OCC.</span></span><br />
<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">They must also respect the following format for their username when registering on the Air Inter website (in order to facilitate recognition of each member connected to the ITVA site):<br />
<br data-end=\"4580\" data-start=\"4577\" />
<strong>IT</strong> followed by the ID number (provided upon registration confirmation), followed by the first name (without spaces or special characters).<br data-end=\"4721\" data-start=\"4718\" />
Example: <strong>IT001Alex</strong></span></span></div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>2.3</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">After acceptance and confirmation of their registration, new members must subscribe to the Air Inter VA Newsletter (Newsletter tab on the main page of the ITVA site).</span></span></div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>2.4</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Pilots are classified into three categories:</span></span></div>

<ul>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Flight Engineer: Corresponding to period 1 – 1982–1997</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Co-pilot: Corresponding to period 2 – 1970–1981</span></span></li>
	<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> Captain: Corresponding to period 3 – 1958–1969</span></span></li>
</ul>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>2.5</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">For members wishing to become instructors, the minimum requirements are as follows:</span></span> <span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<p><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"> </span></span></p>

<ul>
	<li data-end=\"5431\" data-start=\"5223\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">To have significant experience in virtual flight and on the IVAO or VATSIM network, to have completed specific training on the relevant aircraft type(s), and to have the agreement of all staff members.<br />
	Or</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"5536\" data-start=\"5434\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">To have real-world experience as a flight instructor (i.e. holding an ICAO instructor license).<br />
	Or</span></span></li>
	<li data-end=\"5601\" data-start=\"5539\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">To have been a real pilot or flight engineer with Air Inter.</span></span><br />
	&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
</div>

<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><strong><span style=\"text-decoration: underline\">3-ADMINISTRATION</span></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>3.1</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">For administrative functions within Air Inter Virtual Airlines, only company management (commonly referred to as staff members) may approve or refuse recruitment. Any recruitment will be made public through the website and/or the forum and/or the “Air Inter Newsletter” and/or by email.</span></span></p>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>3.2</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">After receiving flight reports, the company will update, within a maximum of 7 days (except in cases of force majeure), the website, the various required processing tasks, and will validate (where applicable and after verification) the PIREP reports</span></span>.</div>

<div style=\"margin: 0in 0in 0pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>3.3</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">If necessary and/or upon request to a staff member, an exemption for all or part of one or more clauses of these regulations may, after acceptance, be granted.</span></span><br />
<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>3.4</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Air Inter Virtual Airlines will keep its members informed of all decisions taken and of company news, its relationships, partnerships, virtual customer demand, etc., through the website and/or the forum and/or the “Air Inter Newsletter” and/or by email.</span></span></div>

<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"><br />
<strong>3.5</strong> -&nbsp;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\">Air Inter Virtual Airlines reserves the right to modify, add, suspend one or more clauses of these regulations and/or parts of the website and/or the status of one or more members, without prior notice.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;\"></span></span><br />
<span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt;\"><br />
